WEBVTT

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.780
Yuzu is alive!

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.400
I believed that was what Sora 
was trying to tell me.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.910
So I was able to shake off my hesitation 
and focus on the duel with Shinji.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.060
But Shinji's fierce attacks,

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:20.100
trying to incite the Commons into revolting against 
the Tops, had my back against the wall.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:20.730
Just then...

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.570
Of course! That's what you wanted!

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.620
Lend me your aid once more, Tuning Magician!

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.440
Synchro Summon!

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.640
Level 8 Enlightenment Paladin!

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.190
Yuya just performed a Synchro Summon!

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.630
D-Wheels.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:04.780
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.490
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:09.930
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.100
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:51.020
A Reunion Across Dimensions

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:54.440
Dodging buffeting attacks from Shinji,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.770
Yuya Sakaki seizes victory, 
in an incredible turnaround.

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:01.050
He's now returning to the Duel Palace!

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.630
Yuya!

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:05.910
Yuzu!

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.760
That was an incredible duel!

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:15.800
You really put that Commons duelist, ranting about 
revolution and uprising, in his place!

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:16.580
Huh?

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.280
How dare you take out Shinji...

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.750
How dare you take out our friend?

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:26.780
Yuya Sakaki, who took out Shinji 
who fought for us, is against us!

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.120
That much is clear!

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.630
He's a shameless enemy, 
currying favor with the Tops!

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:33.230
Enemy? No!

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.020
Hey, wait...

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:38.510
That was an incredible duel, which made 
our palms sweat till its end.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.330
Interpreting it that way is such a waste!

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:43.720
You Tops... You Commons, too...

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.950
Let's applaud the victor together.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.070
That's what the Friendship Cup is about!

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:49.760
That's right!

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.540
We should celebrate Yuya Sakaki 
from the bottom of our hearts.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.870
Shut up!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.280
Get our enemy off the field!

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.730
Great job, Yuya Sakaki!

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:01.290
Die, Yuya Sakaki!

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.510
That duel just now...

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:10.610
In order to reach Jack, I did put 
winning over entertaining.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:13.530
As a result, instead of bringing smiles,

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.350
I created an even wider gap between 
the Tops and Commons.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.110
Did I do the right thing?

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:29.700
Damn!

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:37.620
Roget...

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.090
Why is the Public Order Bureau's director here?

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.560
Brilliantly done.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.610
Your magnificent duel impressed me.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:53.360
Particularly, that elegant and daring Pendulum 
into Synchro Summon at the end...

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:56.730
I actually uttered a cry of excitement.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:01.780
No wonder I sponsored you, Yuya Sakaki.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.150
Hey, you!

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:06.990
What does he mean, he sponsored you?

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:10.390
Is he saying you've been connected to security...

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.460
to the Tops' dogs, from the start?

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:18.140
Did he declare you Jack's first opponent as part

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:20.740
of some behind-the-scenes deal, too?

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.570
Deal?!

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:28.540
Yuya Sakaki's backdoor dealings with 
the Public Order Bureau's director

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:31.820
led to being selected as the king's opponent?

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:34.550
Is this a big scoop?

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:38.030
W-Wait a minute... What are 
you talking about, Shinji?

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:42.240
That was the first time I ever met Roget, 
and I was with you the whole—

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.520
I thought something was fishy here!

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:49.660
Some nobody duelist would never 
be chosen as the king's opponent!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:53.470
What did he give you in exchange 
for the duel with Jack?

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:57.670
In exchange for losing, were you promised 
you wouldn't be sent underground?

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:01.640
Hearing someone like you prattle on about 
how this tournament is wrong...

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:04.110
What a laugh!

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:05.840
What's going on, Yuya?

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.730
I told you, that isn't—

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.840
Of course it isn't true...

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.250
There has been no such backdoor deal.

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:15.060
Right?

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.020
I simply believed in his potential. That's all.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.250
Potential?!

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.500
Indeed, he is a nobody.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:28.480
But Yuya Sakaki had the Pendulum Summon,

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.620
a power not even we knew about.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:36.720
I thought the best way to learn the extent 
of that power would be for him

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:41.110
to fight City's greatest duelist, Jack Atlas.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:47.150
Naturally, the duel ended in Jack's victory.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:52.570
But now I see that my judgment 
of Yuya Sakaki at the time

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:53.860
was not mistaken.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.270
With every fight, he becomes stronger!

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:02.300
This time, he succeeded in going from 
Pendulum to Synchro Summon.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:06.070
Yuya Sakaki has already evolved as a duelist!

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.040
Look...

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:12.330
So many of those spectators feel as I do.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.510
We hope for but one thing.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:19.450
For you to win the Friendship Cup,

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:22.490
to fight Jack Atlas once more!

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:29.130
I'm counting on you, Yuya.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:31.660
Wait a minute!

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:35.550
After the second match of the 
Friendship Cup's second day,

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:41.580
Yuya Sakaki, favorite of Security Director 
Roget, scored a brilliant win...

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.680
Why would Roget go to such lengths?

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.980
Singing Yuya Sakaki's praises?

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.600
Is he trying to get Yuya on his side?

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.130
No need to worry.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.820
He is Yusyo Sakaki's son.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.290
He would not be that foolish.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:03.900
Yuya...

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.680
Yuya's working with the Tops?

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.570
It can't be... Why?

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:15.180
I thought he understood my feelings.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:19.080
The feeling of the Commons, 
looked down on by the Tops.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.280
My feelings of being looked down on by Jack.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.140
That's why I gave him that card.

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:29.820
I wanted him to fight Jack again, win,

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:32.890
and throw that card in his face.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:37.500
But he was with the Tops from the start.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:39.310
This is—

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:40.330
This is ridiculous!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:43.030
Potential? Evolution?

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:46.500
Then, this was a fixed race all along!

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:48.410
A fixed race?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:52.520
My! Another accusation!

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:57.360
If this is true, the tournament's 
very foundation is in question!

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:02.220
Acting once again as Top City TV's 
top reporter, Melissa Claire,

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:05.240
I will directly interview Director Roget, 
to learn the truth—

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:09.070
You are the one being ridiculous,

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:10.700
Shinji Weber.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.200
What?

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:18.300
After all, if your duel with Yuya 
had been a fixed race,

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:23.540
then you, who lost to Yuya, 
would be part of that conspiracy...

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:28.120
You lost to Yuya in a fair fight.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:32.150
You're just whining because 
you don't want to admit it.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:33.240
I...

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.960
You are an eyesore! Remove the 
loser from the venue at once!

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:43.400
Damn... Let me go!

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.230
This isn't over, Yuya!

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:47.430
I swear I'll make you pay for this!

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:49.900
Shinji! No, listen to me!

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:50.640
My resentment...

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:53.610
Crow will inherit it and avenge me!

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:55.670
Shinji...

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.100
Shinji, I'm going to save you!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:01.690
Even if you're underground, don't give up!

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:03.770
You hear me, Shinji?!

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.360
Let me go!

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:14.280
I need to go!

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.820
Yuzu's been found!

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:17.910
So I need to get to her!

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:20.870
Release him.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:23.220
Yes. sir.

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:26.710
It's a scoop... A scoop!

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:34.220
Um, it's okay for the loser to leave 
the venue, but the winner?

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:35.310
Are you sure?

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:40.090
He isn't being taken back to the penthouse...

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:43.450
Because he really is with the Tops?

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:46.920
I won't abandon my friend.

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:49.050
I decided to win, so I wouldn't have to!

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:54.170
I swore I'd win, to make both 
Tops and Commons smile!

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:03.080
I'm sure I saw Sora around here.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:05.230
Where is he? Where are you?

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:07.660
Sora! Hey!

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:09.210
Where are you?

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:12.900
Come out! You're there, aren't you, Sora?

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:23.320
Sora! Where are you?!

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:26.900
Answer me, Sora!

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:30.370
Sora! Hey, Sora!

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:35.310
Sora!

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:37.380
Hush. You're being followed.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:39.980
Come this way, quickly.

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:41.370
Where's Yuzu?

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:43.520
She's here, right? She's safe, right?

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:44.780
Quiet down.

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:46.480
She isn't?

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:51.530
Weren't you telling me that Yuzu's alive?

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:53.060
We'll talk later.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.210
Yuzu's safe.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:16.700
No need to worry. For now, I'm hiding 
her somewhere safe.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:18.700
Thank goodness...

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:21.760
You saved me, huh?

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.930
Thanks. I mean it.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:30.240
But I really was surprised to learn you were 
in the Synchro Dimension, too.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:31.600
Same here.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:36.600
I never thought I'd see you in another dimension.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:39.210
After what happened in the battle royal...

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:41.410
The battle royal...

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:47.880
We haven't seen each other since then, have we?

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:58.690
Back then, you said you had something 
more important than friendship, right?

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:00.500
Yes, I did.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:04.870
We have an important mission, to unite the world.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:08.170
I still feel the same way.

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:11.610
Is that why you've come to the 
Synchro Dimension?

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:16.640
Does that mean Academia is already 
attacking this dimension, too?

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:21.640
You're about to do something awful here, 
like you did to the Xyz Dimension...

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:23.700
To Kurosaki and Ute's home?

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:28.590
Don't tell me... You came to kidnap Yuzu?

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.320
Dennis was also from Academia.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:36.660
He infiltrated the Xyz Dimension to kidnap Ruri,

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.960
Kurosaki's little sister.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:41.580
Is that why you're here, Sora?

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:44.640
Did you come to our dimension to kidnap Yuzu—

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:45.700
No!

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:54.550
However, the higher-ups may have 
learned about Yuzu from my memory.

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:56.150
But still, I swear to you...

00:13:56.470 --> 00:14:00.620
I didn't come to Standard to kidnap Yuzu.

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:04.860
And I came to the Synchro Dimension 
to save Yuzu, as well!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:06.590
To save her?

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:10.330
I'm not Yuzu.

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:13.830
Can it be?

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:19.210
Back then, I thought someone from 
the Obelisk Force I'd come with

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:23.370
had accidentally taken Yuzu to 
Academia, instead of her.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:26.730
Accidentally? Confusing her with Serena?

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:30.320
Yes. It would have been natural 
for someone on my team,

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:37.230
with orders from the Professor to take back 
Serena, to have made a mistake.

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.460
So I quickly returned to Academia.

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:47.980
But no matter how I searched, 
I couldn't find Yuzu anywhere.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:53.340
Yuzu Hiiragi escaped, you say?

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:58.580
Then, for the first time,

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:03.370
I learned that the Professor didn't 
want only Serena, but Yuzu, too.

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:06.740
But why?

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:11.910
Why is this Professor collecting 
girls like Yuzu and Serena?

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:15.080
Answer me, Sora!

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.530
I'm telling you, I don't know!

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:21.500
I was only ordered to bring back Serena.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:24.000
They didn't tell me why.

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:29.210
But even if I don't know why,

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:32.480
I have to do what the Professor orders.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.340
That is the rule at Academia.

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:41.990
So I decided to return to the Standard 
Dimension and search for Serena.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:46.580
I thought there was a chance Yuzu 
might still be in that dimension.

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:52.080
That was when I learned that Reiji 
Akaba was leading a force,

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.170
called the Lancers, across dimensions.

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:57.860
And that you and Serena were part of it.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.440
That's why you came to the Synchro Dimension?

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:06.180
Yes, and then I heard Dennis's confession.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:11.020
The man involved in the Ruri 
incident probably joined

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:13.690
the Lancers to keep an eye on Serena.

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:19.430
To keep him away from Serena, 
I returned him to Academia.

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:21.840
To Academia?!

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:24.750
But they'll learn Yuzu and Serena are here!

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.000
They'd learn soon enough, regardless!

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:32.300
Sooner or later, the Obelisk Force will arrive.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.770
To get Serena and Yuzu.

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:39.240
Serena's from Academia, like me.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:44.780
I have no interest in disobeying the 
Professor's order to bring her back.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:47.350
But Yuzu...

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:56.190
Do you remember before, 
when you asked if I'd taught

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:59.550
Fusion Summoning to Yuzu because 
I regard her as a friend?

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:01.530
Yeah.

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:04.230
At the time, I denied it.

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:06.140
But the truth is...

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:13.010
I was raised at Academia. I'd never had a friend.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:17.940
Everyone's so desperate to 
become the ultimate warrior.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:22.850
We never joke around or laugh together...

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:28.330
Which meant you and Yuzu were my first...

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:29.910
Sora...

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:33.450
That's why I really want to save Yuzu, at least!

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:38.040
I don't want Yuzu in the prison 
that is Academia.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:41.510
So I have a proposal for you.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:46.210
Bring Serena to the place where I have Yuzu.

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:47.520
Serena?

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:51.060
You know where she is now, right?

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.920
If I bring Serena, what will you do to her?

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:56.360
Give her to me.

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.490
In exchange, I'll give you Yuzu,

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:01.890
and you can take her back to 
the Standard Dimension!

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.060
You want me to abandon Serena?

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:05.360
No!

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:09.130
I told you, she's from Academia 
in the first place!

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.870
I'm just taking her back!

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:13.100
To "the prison that is Academia"?

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:16.270
I won't abandon Serena to a place like that!

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:17.750
Or Yuzu!

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:21.210
And I'll save Ruri from it, too!

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:23.380
I won't let the Professor do as he likes.

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:25.900
I see.

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:28.810
That boy has Yuzu Hiiragi.

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:34.630
If Dennis is already back at Academia,

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:38.100
it's only a matter of time until they send Joeri!

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.000
I have no time to spare!

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:45.170
Seize the boy with Yuya Sakaki, at once.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:49.640
I shall personally interrogate him 
to learn Yuzu Hiiragi's location.

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:51.870
Try to understand, Yuya!

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:55.350
This is the only way to save Yuzu!

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:58.200
If you hesitate, the Obelisk Force will come.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:00.430
And this city will become a battlefield, too!

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:04.260
By that logic, if I take Yuzu, won't the 
Obelisk Force come?

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:08.060
And our home will still become a battlefield.

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:11.420
I'll also be endangering my friends 
at the You Show School.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.430
I won't let that happen!

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:18.120
Preventing that is why I'm taking Serena 
back, to convince the Professor—

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:21.370
You know very well you can't convince him!

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:26.940
Academia needs to be defeated.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:30.430
If you're going to work, work for that!

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:32.660
You need to wake up soon, Sora.

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:36.490
Look out!

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:38.550
Yuya!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:42.380
Go, Sora! Protect Yuzu!

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:50.000
I'm counting on you, Sora.

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:58.320
What am I doing here?

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:00.620
I remember dueling Sergey...

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.400
I'm still a little dizzy.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.440
Are you okay?

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:12.340
Hey, it's the girl who was 
thrown from the duel lane.

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:16.930
But I'm surprised you survived 
a fall from that height...

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.210
I fell?

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:23.210
I see...

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:27.370
I'm sorry. I don't really remember.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:30.470
Speaking of which, did you see Yuya?

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:33.340
You know Yuya?

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:35.680
Yeah, Crow saved him!

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:39.030
And Serena and Layra and...

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:41.830
Huh? What was the last guy's name?

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:49.080
Who cares? He's just a fart in the wind.

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:54.430
Anyway, Crow's a nice guy, 
so he'll save anyone!

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.170
I see.

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:59.800
That Crow man saved Yuya and the others.

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:01.910
Hey, we can't stay here.

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:05.120
Crow's duel is about to start!

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:07.600
Come with us to cheer him on.

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:09.230
Me, too?

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:13.290
We can't get to the Duel Palace 
because they're watching

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.520
for fake tickets after the last time...

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:17.310
But we know City.

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:19.480
We have a special place to watch from.

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:23.540
Of course, security can't find 
us there! Come on, hurry!

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:27.000
W-Wait!

00:21:30.610 --> 00:21:34.940
If what Shinji said was true, Yuya's a traitor, too!

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:37.850
I can't trust anyone, anymore.

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.410
My only choice is to win.

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:45.190
I seriously have to win... And beat Jack!

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:53.360
Dennis can't be alone...

00:21:53.360 --> 00:21:57.560
Other Academia spies are here.

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:01.160
I will sniff them all out.

00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:06.000
The third match of the Friendship 
Cup's third day is...

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:12.440
Crow Hogan versus Syun Kurosaki!

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:52.960
Sora! Take care... Take care of Yuzu!

00:23:52.960 --> 00:23:55.420
Why is security so strict?

00:23:55.420 --> 00:23:58.350
I need to get back to Yuzu already!

00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:00.950
Academia has infiltrated from multiple angles.

00:24:01.360 --> 00:24:03.950
If you're with them, I'll show no mercy.

00:24:03.950 --> 00:24:07.070
I'll win and avenge my comrade!

00:24:07.070 --> 00:24:10.290
Shinji isn't the only one who 
can unite the Commons!

00:24:11.040 --> 00:24:15.150
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Each Person's Battlefield.

00:24:15.150 --> 00:24:17.180
The fun is only getting started!
